## 🚀 Getting Started Locally

### Prerequisites
- Node.js (v18+)
- MongoDB Atlas account
- Razorpay account (test mode keys)

### 1. Clone the repository
```bash
git clone https://github.com/lingeswaran-07/Foody.git
cd Foody
```

### 2. Backend Setup
```bash
cd Backend
npm install
```
Create a `.env` file in `Backend/`:
```env
MONGO_URI=your_mongodb_connection_string
JWT_SECRET=your_jwt_secret
RAZORPAY_KEY_ID=your_razorpay_key_id
RAZORPAY_KEY_SECRET=your_razorpay_key_secret
```
Run the server:
```bash
npm start
```

### 3. Frontend Setup
```bash
cd ../frontend
npm install
npm run dev
```

### 4. Admin Panel Setup
```bash
cd ../admin
npm install
npm run dev
```

##  Environment Variables

 Variable 

 `MONGO_URI` -- MongoDB Atlas connection string (include database name) 
 `JWT_SECRET` -- Secret key for signing JWT tokens 
 `RAZORPAY_KEY_ID` -- Razorpay public API key 
 `RAZORPAY_KEY_SECRET` -- Razorpay secret key (server-side only) 

